**/config/local.yaml
**/config/*.local.yaml
# NOTE: config/production.yaml is deliberately tracked (not ignored),
# matching the family's other services (person/worker/place/thing/
# event/course). It holds no secret directly — every credential is a
# Tera `{{ get_env(name="…") }}` call resolved from the environment at
# boot, never a literal value — so there is nothing here that needs to
# stay untracked. This crate's own loco scaffold ignored it by default
# (`**/config/production.yaml`, removed here); that meant the file
# never left this machine — see examples/compose/ (DEP-1) and this
# crate's own Dockerfile, both of which need it to exist on a fresh
# checkout. (Sibling crates organization/care-pathway/case/portfolio/
# authentication had the same gitignore rule hiding a real boot-time
# bug in their production.yaml; this crate's has no mailer block, so
# it wasn't affected, but the same "never leaves this machine" problem
# still applied.)

# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/

# include cargo lock
!Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
